.TH "shrinkSpace" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
shrinkSpace \- reclaim free space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.shrinkSpace([options])\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Sdb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to reclaim the free space of all files under the specified
collection space.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
options ( \f[I]object, optional\f[] )
.PP
Modify the collection space to be reclaimed and the command position parameters
through the parameter "options":
.IP \[bu] 2
CollectionSpace ( \f[I]string\f[] ): Collection space name.
.RS 2
.PP
If this parameter is not specified, all free space under the collection space
will be reclaimed by default.
.PP
Format: \f[C]CollectionSpace: "sample"\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Location Elements ( \f[I]object\f[] ): Command positional parameters.
.RS 2
.PP
If this parameter is not specified, it will be executed globally by default.
.PP
Format: \f[C]GroupName: "db1"\f[]
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, there is no return value.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
The common exceptions of \f[C]shrinkSpace()\f[] function are as follows:
.PP
